{"type":"text","timestamp":1787405219175,"sessionID":"ses_fd65a87edffe1C1CY3NqP4X610","part":{"id":"prt_029a72cf70019GKAQ40gcMCZLK","messageID":"msg_029a71b830014d16lqJ97CDA3F","sessionID":"ses_fd65a87edffe1C1CY3NqP4X610","type":"text","text":"Confirmed: the 5 option-test failures are pre-existing and unrelated to `argument.js` (they fail identically without my change). My change doesn't regress anything.\n\nThe `Argument` class is now fully reimplemented:\n- Constructor parses `<name>` (required), `[name]` (optional), bare name (required), and trailing `...` (variadic), with `name()` returning the bare name.\n- `default()`, `argParser()`, `choices()`, `argRequired()`, `argOptional()` all return `this` for chaining.\n- `choices()` copies the array (`slice()`) and installs a `parseArg` that throws `InvalidArgumentError(\"Allowed choices are a, b.\")` for invalid values and accumulates via `_collectValue` when variadic.\n- `_collectValue(value, previous)` starts a new array when `previous` isn't an array (or is the default) and appends otherwise.\n- `humanReadableArgName` already renders `<name>`, `[name]`, `<name...>`, `[name...]`.","time":{"start":1787405217015,"end":1787405219171}}}
